  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>N</mi></math> be the set of natural numbers and a relation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>N</mi></math> be defined by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>:</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>.&nbsp;Then the relation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> is",
    "image": null
  },
